  "sourceDisposition": "Partial I10.preparation assertions under accounts/decks/lobby D-189/D-191/D-202/D-203/D-221/D-293/D-294 and server authority/recovery D-259/D-275/D-278/D-285/D-289. This unit completes native transfer/inspection/feedback/row-transition and affected existing-session integration. Source assignments remain whole-scenario accounting, not invented passes for Ready/start/play-sideboard, full lifecycle, rematch, physical/device matrices or final UI comparison.",
  "implementationNotes": [
    "Preparation uses I10b1 capture/transfer and same shared/ordered per-card semantics without a new processor, queue, mutation endpoint or all-command. One pointer owns an immutable capture from down through release; recognized drag suppresses tap. Connected/lobby checks, native disjoint compact targets, full-row custom actions, disabled/read-only presentation, row keys and removal disposal prevent action retargeting or ghost activation. Thumbnail/name inspection cannot receive handle input.",
    "Controller feedback compares previous and next displayed section membership, so actual partial moves and reverse reconciliation replace the text; receipt/result counts are not displayed as acceptance. A permanent 40dp slot and standard 1.5s Animatable fade never move list headers. Standard Compose 180ms item placement/fade retargets current layout, removes semantics immediately and does not delay counts/sending. Android instrumentation retains visible/faded/removed endpoints and exact bounds; normal accessibility remains meaningful after visual fade.",
    "Two real normal APKs create all synthetic business state through native UI. Setup and portrait taps are retained in the configured diagnostic before the missing-scroll check; portrait drags are retained before observer cwd failure. The passing retained tail does not reset or repeat those actions; it completes outside-drop, landscape, missing-art inspection, other-device captured-copy conflict, paused-service prediction and reopen/server-first restart. Separate actual Android checks exercise native accessibility/feedback/row animation/cancel and rapid pointer removal without replacing the normal-app journey.",
    "Infrastructure/check-only diagnostics: explicit exact owned-peer records satisfy the existing ADB discovery guard; redundant owned APK readbacks are preserved off tmpfs with hashes; explicit /prism/ debug catalog configuration and guarded APK reattachment repair native setup; re-find the named handle after scrolling rather than dragging the returned container; observer root cwd/table and rejection-outbox expectations use actual schema; instrumentation navigates/waits for Games normally. No runtime repair was needed after the first affected source build. Final E2E test-only deletion removes an unexercised nonchecking done branch; affected test compilation passes, and exact executed-stage source identity is retained separately from that final deletion."
  ],
  "remainingObligations": [
